  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study constructs a multidimensional Environmental Stress Index for Barcelona by applying Geographically Weighted Principal Component Analysis to six environmental variables across 1,068 census tracts. The analysis reveals that 45% of the city's population resides in high-stress areas, which are concentrated in central, eastern, and northern districts covering just 25% of the municipal territory.",
      "why": "It replaces uniform, city-wide environmental assessments with a localized weighting system that identifies which specific stressors dominate in different neighborhoods, allowing planners to target interventions to distinct local inequalities."
